      "writtenOn": "2025-02-04T01:16:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we allow the for-loop to run through the end so that `hid_available`, `hogp_available`, and `headtracker_available` can all be populated?\n\nOtherwise, if `headtracker_available` is put in front of `hogp_available`, you will break early and not updating `hogp_available` to its correct value\n\nAnd if `headtracker_available` and `hogp_available` are always or\u0027ed together in subsequent code, then it is ok to return early, but you should create a new variable like \"le_hid_available \u003d hogp_available || headtracker_available` and use that in follow-up code instead\n\nIMO, letting that for-loop runnign through the end is eaasier.",
